<title>INDIA: Japan clears India HLL's fish paste plant.</title>
<headline>Japan clears India HLL's fish paste plant.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unilever's Indian subsidiary Hindustan Lever Ltd (HLL) said its surimi (fish paste) factory has cleared Japanese quality audit.</p>
<p>&quot;The All-Japan Kamaboko (fish products) Makers Association has certified that the HLL plant meets the stringent standards of that country,&quot; HLL said in a statement.</p>
<p>It is the second such facility in the world to clear Japanese quality audit, the company said.</p>
<p>HLL's surimi factory at Chorwad in the western Gujarat state was set up in collaboration with Shinto Corporation of Japan. The produce is exported to Japan.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
